---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const chapters = [
  ['Work and standing', 'the tenth, sixth and eleventh'],
  ['Money', 'the second and eleventh'],
  ['Marriage and partnership', 'the seventh and second'],
  ['Children and creative work', 'the fifth and ninth'],
  ['Home and property', 'the fourth'],
  ['Body and health', 'the first and sixth'],
  ['Mind and temperament', 'the first, fourth and fifth'],
  ['Fortune and support', 'the ninth and eleventh'],
  ['Family and siblings', 'the third and fourth'],
  ['Dharma and inward life', 'the ninth and twelfth'],
];
---

<Base title="Phalita">
  <header class="hero">
    <p class="kicker">फल · phalita</p>
    <h1>Your chart, read the way an astrologer reads it.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Ten chapters on your life — work, money, marriage, children, home, body,
      mind, fortune, family and dharma. Every line is a condition Phaladīpikā
      states, tested against your chart, and every line carries its verse.
    </p>
    <a class="cta" href="./reading">Read your chart <span>→</span></a>
  </header>

  <section class="sample">
    <p class="kicker">What a chapter reads like</p>
    <div class="excerpt">
      <p class="sample-title">Money <span>the second and eleventh</span></p>
      <p>
        Money is one of the well-placed parts of this chart. It accumulates, and
        it accumulates from things you already hold rather than from windfalls.
      </p>
      <p>
        You keep what you earn; your word carries weight in money matters and you
        see a financial situation before others do.
      </p>
      <p>
        The leak is worth naming anyway. Money leaves through obligations rather
        than through spending, and family resources do not back you when you need
        them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Build slowly and keep what you build. This is not a chart that rewards a
        big bet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="what">
    <h2>The ten chapters</h2>
    <ul class="chapters">
      {chapters.map(([title, strap]) => (
        <li><strong>{title}</strong><span>{strap}</span></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="how">
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>You give a birth date, time and place.</li>
      <li>The chart is computed — sidereal positions, houses, strengths, daśā.</li>
      <li>Every condition the text states is tested against that chart.</li>
      <li>What fires is written into prose. What contradicts itself is shown as contradicting itself.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="rules">
    <h2>What it will not do</h2>
    <p>
      It will not give you a death date. The classical arithmetic is disputed by
      the tradition itself — 22.24 records that Bhadanta rejected the piṇḍāyu and
      Varāhamihira agreed — and a figure from a disputed method is worse than none.
    </p>
    <p>
      It will not pronounce a grave reading from one placement. Phaladīpikā 15.6
      states that two or three conditions must agree before a severe loss is
      declared; where they do not, the engine says it is withholding the reading
      rather than guessing at it.
    </p>
    <p>
      It will not show you a chart. That is what a calculation platform is for;
      this one answers in words.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
